      "notes": "Evaluated under profile painter-12.1-isolated-half-alpha (decision 044). The masks are exact: every texel where the child's mask (a ramp along y) is 1 or 0 equals both recordings, and the sRGB8 maps are exact: the group coverage (255 + y)/510 lies half-way between two 8-bit codes on even rows, and Painter stores the code of its binary16 value (up on rows y mod 64 >= 32, down elsewhere), the profile's sRGB8 coverage rule; the float32 value stored all ties down (3 709 values off). On the RGB32F row where the child's mask is 0 the uniform's float32 value reproduces the recordings (the profile's plain 32-bit float operand; 1 + (v - 1) leaves 8 values off). The RGB32F and RGB16 residual lies where the child's mask is strictly between 0 and 1: the uniform Screen fill above it composites over a partly covered backdrop inside the group, the source-over whose float32 operation order is not identified (phase1.10_compositor-float32-residual, parity/reports/phase1/compositor-float32-residual.md); a divergence, no exception proposed (the owner's decision)."
    },
